# .gitignore — added alongside the docker-compose setup (SPEC-SDLC-4-ADDENDUM-2). Everything here
# is generated at boot/build time, never source: log files, temp/cache (bootsnap, pids), the SQLite
# database files themselves (config/database.yml points these at storage/, never db/ — see that
# file's comment), Bundler's local config, and Node's install output for the optional Lighthouse CI
# gate (README.md §3). The root repo .gitignore already covers *.sqlite3/.env globally; the entries
# below are Rails-specific paths that ignore applies to but doesn't name directly.
/log/*
/tmp/*
!/log/.keep
!/tmp/.keep
/storage/*
!/storage/.keep
/.bundle/
/public/assets/
/node_modules/
